          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em end
            is a special kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            of the form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C^{op} \times C \to D
            (sometimes called a
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bifunctor"} bifunctor
          %p
            If we think of such a functor in the sense of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/profunctors"} profunctors
            as encoding a left and right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            on the object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\prod_{c \in C} F(c,c),
          %p
            then the
            %em end
            of the functor picks out the universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            on which the left and right actions coincide. Dually, the
            %em coend
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is the universal quotient of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi C
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{c \in C} F(c,c)
            that forces the two actions of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            on that object to be equal.
          %p
            A classical example of an
            %em end
            is the
            = succeed "-object" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            between
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limits"} weighted limits
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+colimits"} weighted colimits
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#in_ordinary_category_theory In ordinary category theory
          %h4#definition_via_extranatural_transformations Definition via extranatural transformations
          %p
            In ordinary
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: C^{op} \times C \to X
            %strong end
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+construction"} universal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extranatural+transformation"} extranatural transformation
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \to e
            which respects the extranatural transformations.
          %p
            In more detail: the end of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is traditionally denoted
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int_{c: C} F(c, c)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_c: \int_{c: C} F(c, c) \to F(c, c),
          %p
            are called the
            %em projection maps
            of the end. Then, given any extranatural transformation with components
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_c: x \to F(c, c),
          %p
            there exists a unique map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi x
                  %mo →
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: x \to e
            such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi c
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta_c = \pi_c f
          %p
            for every object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            The notion of
            %strong coend
            is dual to the notion of end. The coend of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            is written
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo :
                        %mi C
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int^{c: C} F(c, c)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo :
                      %mi C
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_c \colon F(c,c) \to \int^{c: C} F(c,c).
          %h4#explicit_definition Explicit definition
          %p We unwrap the definition of an extranatural transformation to obtain a more explicit description of an end.
          #wedge.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: C^{op} \times C \to X
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
              %strong wedge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mi w
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e: w \to F
              %strong over F
              is an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
              and maps
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi w
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e_c: w\to F(c, c)
              for each object
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mo →
                      %mi c
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: c \to c'
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi w
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi e
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi c
                                    %mo ′
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo ′
                            %mo ,
                            %mi c
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi e
                                    %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi F
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi f
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mi c
                                  %mo ′
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi c
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi c
                                %mo ,
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi c
                            %mo ,
                            %mi c
                            %mo ′
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    w &amp; \overset{e_{c'}}{\to} &amp; F(c', c')\\
                    ^\mathllap{e_c}\downarrow &amp; &amp; \downarrow^\mathrlap{F(f, c')}\\
                    F(c, c) &amp; \underset{F(c, f)}{\to} &amp; F(c, c')
                    }
          %p
            Given a wedge
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo :
                  %mi w
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e: w \to F
            and a map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi v
                    %mo →
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: v \to w
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi v
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e f: v \to F
            by composition. We define the end as follows:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo ×
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: C^{op} \times C \to X
              be a functor. An
              %strong end
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is a universal wedge over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mi w
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e: w \to F
              such that each other wedge
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi w
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e': w' \to F
              factors through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              via a unique map
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo ′
                      %mo →
                      %mi w
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w' \to w
          %p
            Dually, a cowedge is given by maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi w
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(c, c) \to w
            satisfying similar commutativity conditions, and a coend is a universal cowedge.
          %h4#ends_as_right_adjoint_functors Ends as right adjoint functors
          %p
            In complete analogy to how
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            are right adjoint functors to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+functor"} diagonal functor
            for the diagram, ends are right adjoint functors to the hom functor.
          %p
            In more detail, suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            are categories.
          %p
            If every diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^{op}\times C\to X
            admits an end, then we have a functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi end
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Fun
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} end\colon Fun(C^{op}\times C,X)\to X
          %p whose left adjoint is the hom functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Fun
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom\colon X\to Fun(C^{op}\times C,X)
          %p
            that sends an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            to the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hom(x)\colon C^{op}\times C\to X
            that sends
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c,d)
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %mi hom
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi c
                        %mo ,
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \coprod_{hom(c,d)}x=hom(c,d)\otimes x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x^{hom(c,d)}
            instead.)
          %p This immediately implies a Fubini theorem for ends and coends.
          %h3#in_enriched_category_theory In enriched category theory
          %p
            There is a definition of
            %em end
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            as follows.
          %h4#end_of_valued_functors
            End of
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            be a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is also
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed monoidal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            may be considered as
            = succeed "-enriched." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi op
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: C^{op} \otimes C \to V
            is a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
          %p
            Then there is a covariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{c, d, e}: F(c, d) \otimes C(d, e) \to F(c, e),
          %p
            (where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(d, e)
            is customary notation for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi hom
                    %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom_C(d, e)
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            in
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                      %mo ,
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                  %mo :
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_{c, d, e}: F(d, e) \otimes C(c, d) \to F(c, e).
          %p
            In detail, the covariant action is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
            of the morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (F(c,-)
                  \\colon
                  C(d,e) \to [F(c,d), F(c,e)])
                  \\in
                  Hom_V(C(d,e),[F(c,d), F(c,e)])
          %p
            under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} Hom-adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Hom_V(C(d,e),[F(c,d), F(c,e)])
                  \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                  Hom_V(C(d,e)\otimes F(c,d),F(c,e))
          %p
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Even if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              is not closed monoidal, we can still define a
              %strong notion
              of covariant
              = succeed "-action," do
